	*** RESOLVED BUGS ***


	*** Originally submitted by Quan Tran in 10/2015 - FIXED 2025-12-23

	Dont miss his improved Go version of SubC at:
	https://github.com/qeedquan/gosubc

	The SubC bootstrap compiler generated by gcc/clang was using
	4-byte int for Value and node args, causing truncation of
	integer literals outside the 32-bit range on x86_64.

	FIX: Changed Value, Q_val, node.args, and related functions
	(mkleaf, mkunop1, mkunop2, mkbinop1, mkbinop2, genlit, cglit)
	from int to long. Now 64-bit integer literals are correctly
	handled even when bootstrapping with gcc/clang.

